    "https://careers.usi.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-of-nursing-evansville-indiana-united-states-195fd611-260c-4b30-b518-1a10d5e4fcd1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Nursing",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Nursing - Evansville, Indiana, United States Applicant Login | My Profile Home (current) USI Benefits About USI EEO is the Law E-Verify Employer Annual Security and Fire Safety Report Application or Interview Accommodation Virtual Campus Tour Academics Athletics Meet the HR Department Kiosk mode It's great to be a Screaming Eagle! Previous Next Assistant Professor of Nursing 494306 Evansville, Indiana, United States Faculty (Full-Time) Add to favorites View favorites Title: Assistant Professor of Nursing Division: Provost's Office Department: Kinney College of Nursing & Health Professions FLSA Status: Exempt Salary Range: Annual Salary EEO Job Group: 2 C5 Position Summary The University of Southern Indiana seeks applications for a 10-month Assistant Professor of Nursing in the Kinney College of Nursing and Health Professions. The position is tenure track and promotion eligible. The appointment will begin as soon as the position is filled. Duties/Responsibilities This position is responsible for teaching responsibilities in the graduate nursing program. Required Knowledge and Skills Candidates must hold a doctoral degree and an unencumbered Indiana RN (or compact) license. Candidates in the process of completing their doctoral degree will be considered. The successful candidate must possess a doctoral degree by the start date of employment. Regular Work Hours/Travel Requirements Regular work hours are 8:00 am - 4:30 pm. Occasional irregular hours may be required. About USI The University of Southern Indiana is a public higher education institution located on a beautiful 1,400-acre campus in Evansville, IN. We offer employees exceptional benefits! Benefits for this position include: Affordable medical, dental, vision, life and short term and long-term disability insurance plans. Retirement plan where the University makes the total contribution equivalent to 7% of annual salary. Full tuition fee waiver for employees/75% for spouses and dependent children. Accrue up to 10 paid vacation days per fiscal year – accrual increases after 4, 7, and 11 years of service For more information about the benefits that USI offers, please visit www.usi.edu/hr/benefits . About the College The faculty in the Kinney College of Nursing and Health Professions work collaboratively with nursing and other health care professional faculty. The support for faculty’s teaching, practice and scholarship activities are substantially enhanced through grants and other extramural funding. A cutting-edge Clinical Simulation Center is used to enhance student learning and support innovative teaching. The college, in addition to university support, Kinney College's technology team supports online and in-classroom teaching for MSN and DNP program courses. A dedicated Advising Center for the College provides support for student advising and related activities. All programs are fully accredited and have an exemplary record of grant award successes. To learn more about the Kinney College of Nursing and Health Professions, please visit our website at https://health.usi.edu. Application Process Click “Apply Now!” near the top right of this page to complete an application and upload application materials to the attention of the Search Committee Chair. Application materials should include: 1. Letter of application 2. Current curriculum vitae 3. Unofficial transcripts 4. Valid unencumbered Indiana (or compact) RN license Search Committee Chair: If you have questions about the open position, please contact Dr. Gina Schaar, search committee chair, at gschaar@usi.edu. Best Consideration Date: For best consideration, please submit materials by September 26, 2026. Pre-Employment Screening A background check will be required for employment in this position. Authorization to Work in the United States USI may sponsor an employment-related visa for this position. Interview Accommodations Persons with disabilities requiring accommodations in the application and interview process please contact the Associate Director of Human Resources, Constance Hermann, at cjhermann1@usi.edu or (812) 461-5363. Contacting the Associate Director of Human Resources is intended for use in seeking disability-related accommodations only. For general applicant inquiries, contact Human Resources at HumanRes@usi.edu or (812) 464-1815. EEO Statement USI is an Equal Opportunity Employer as to all protected groups, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities Recommended Jobs Assistant Cheer Coach Evansville, Indiana, United States Athletics Assistant Cheer Coach, part-time, non-benefit eligible Human Resources Business Partner Evansville, Indiana, United States Human Resources Human Resources Business Partner, full-time, benefits-eligible Dean, Kinney College of Nursing and Health Professions Evansville, Indiana, United States Kinney College of Nursing & Health Professions Dean, Kinney College of Nursing and Health Professions Assistant Professor of Marketing Evansville, Indiana, United States Romain College of Business 9-month, Tenure track Assistant Professor of Marketing Lecturer in World Languages and Cultures Evansville, Indiana, United States College of Liberal Arts Part-Time Lecturer in World Languages and Cultures Assistant Director of Development Evansville, Indiana, United States Development Full-time, benefits eligible Assistant Director of Development. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Terms & Conditions Privacy Policy Candidate Details"
    },
    "https://careers.usi.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-of-marketing-evansville-indiana-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Marketing",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Marketing - Evansville, Indiana, United States Applicant Login | My Profile Home (current) USI Benefits About USI EEO is the Law E-Verify Employer Annual Security and Fire Safety Report Application or Interview Accommodation Virtual Campus Tour Academics Athletics Meet the HR Department Kiosk mode It's great to be a Screaming Eagle! Previous Next Assistant Professor of Marketing 494319 Evansville, Indiana, United States Faculty (Full-Time) Add to favorites View favorites Title: Assistant Professor of Marketing Division: Provost's Office Department: Romain College of Business FLSA Status: Exempt Salary Range: Annual Salary EEO Job Group: 2 C5 Position Summary The Department of Economics and Marketing in the Romain College of Business at the University of Southern Indiana invites applications for a 9-month tenure-track Assistant Professor of Marketing position to begin in August 2027. Duties/Responsibilities The successful candidate will be expected to teach in the undergraduate Marketing program, with opportunities to teach in the MBA program. Teaching responsibilities will include introduction to marketing and other marketing courses based on department needs. Marketing faculty are expected to pursue innovative teaching practices, maintain an active research program, provide academic advising to marketing students, and provide service at the program, university, and community levels. Required Knowledge and Skills A Ph.D. from an AACSB accredited College of Business with a concentration in Marketing is required. Applicants with ABD status will be considered for the rank of Instructor until degree is completed. About USI The University of Southern Indiana is a public higher education institution located on a beautiful 1,400-acre campus in Evansville, IN. We offer employees exceptional benefits! Benefits for this position include: Affordable medical, dental, vision, life and short term and long-term disability insurance plans. Retirement plan where the University makes the total contribution equivalent to 11% of annual salary. Full tuition fee waiver for employees, spouses, and dependent children. Vacation and sick time Holiday pay Free access to Recreation, Fitness & Wellness Center. Access to on-campus University Health Center and Dental Hygiene Clinic. For more information about the benefits that USI offers, please visit www.usi.edu/hr/benefits . About the Department The Romain College of Business is dual accredited by the AACSB for business and accounting and plays an important role in the economic and social development of the region. The college currently enrolls approximately 1,100 undergraduate business majors across eight different programs and more than 1,000 MBA students across multiple concentrations. The college operates several state-of-the-art labs providing faculty access to high-quality resources for teaching and research. These labs include the Biometrix Discovery Lab which will be part of the college’s new Center for Applied Business Technologies scheduled to open in fall 2026. Application Process Click “Apply Now!” near the top right of this page to complete an application and upload application materials to the attention of the Search Committee Chair. Application materials should include: Letter of application describing relevant experience and interest in the position Current curriculum vitae A statement of teaching philosophy and current research agenda Unofficial transcripts (Official transcripts required at a later stage.) Search Committee Chair: If you have questions about the open position, please contact Dr. Chad Milewicz, search committee chair, at cmmilewicz@usi.edu. Best Consideration Date: For best consideration, please submit materials by September 26, 2026. Pre-Employment Screening A background check will be required for employment in this position. Authorization to Work in the United States USI may sponsor an employment-related visa for this position. Interview Accommodations Persons with disabilities requiring accommodations in the application and interview process please contact the Associate Director of Human Resources, Constance Hermann, at cjhermann1@usi.edu or (812) 461-5363. Contacting the Associate Director of Human Resources is intended for use in seeking disability-related accommodations only. For general applicant inquiries, contact Human Resources at HumanRes@usi.edu or (812) 464-1815. EEO Statement USI is an Equal Opportunity Employer as to all protected groups, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities Recommended Jobs Assistant Cheer Coach Evansville, Indiana, United States Athletics Assistant Cheer Coach, part-time, non-benefit eligible Human Resources Business Partner Evansville, Indiana, United States Human Resources Human Resources Business Partner, full-time, benefits-eligible Dean, Kinney College of Nursing and Health Professions Evansville, Indiana, United States Kinney College of Nursing & Health Professions Dean, Kinney College of Nursing and Health Professions Assistant Professor of Nursing Evansville, Indiana, United States Kinney College of Nursing & Health Professions 10 month, tenure track Assistant Professor of Nursing. Lecturer in World Languages and Cultures Evansville, Indiana, United States College of Liberal Arts Part-Time Lecturer in World Languages and Cultures Assistant Director of Development Evansville, Indiana, United States Development Full-time, benefits eligible Assistant Director of Development. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Terms & Conditions Privacy Policy Candidate Details"
    },
    "https://careers.usi.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-of-social-work-evansville-indiana-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Social Work",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Social Work - Evansville, Indiana, United States Applicant Login | My Profile Home (current) USI Benefits About USI EEO is the Law E-Verify Employer Annual Security and Fire Safety Report Application or Interview Accommodation Virtual Campus Tour Academics Athletics Meet the HR Department Kiosk mode It's great to be a Screaming Eagle! Previous Next Assistant Professor of Social Work 494276 Evansville, Indiana, United States Faculty (Full-Time) Add to favorites View favorites Title: Assistant Professor of Social Work Division: Provost's Office Department: College of Liberal Arts FLSA Status: Exempt Salary Range: Annual Salary EEO Job Group: 2 C5 Position Summary The Department of Social Work at the University of Southern Indiana, a public university in Evansville, Indiana, seeks applications for a 9-month tenure track position at the Assistant Professor level in Social Work. The appointment will begin in Fall 2027. This position requires teaching and responsibilities to be performed on campus. Applicants must be available to teach in person and relocate to the area if not currently residing locally. Duties/Responsibilities The Assistant Professor will be expected to teach 12 credit hours per semester, which includes undergraduate and/or graduate departmental course offerings in Social Work, in addition to advising students, engaging in scholarly activity, and providing professional, university and community service. The Social Work program is Council on Social Work Education (CSWE) accredited. The teaching load for this position will be 4/4. Required Knowledge and Skills Applicants must hold a doctoral degree in Social Work or a closely related field. ABD considered at the rank of Instructor if doctoral degree is not conferred by hire date. Applicants must hold a master’s degree in Social Work from a CSWE accredited program and a minimum of two years post masters experience. About the Department Information on the degree programs in the Department of Social Work may be found at https://www.usi.edu/liberal-arts/social-work. Application Process Click “Apply Now!” near the top right of this page to complete an application and upload application materials to the attention of the Search Committee Chair. Application materials should include: Letter of application addressing relevant experience in teaching and clinical Social Work Current curriculum vitae Unofficial transcripts Brief statement of teaching philosophy Description of research plans Search Committee Chair: If you have questions about the open position, please contact Dr. Wendy Turner, search committee chair, at wturner@usi.edu . Best Consideration Date: For best consideration, please submit materials by September 19, 2026. Pre-Employment Screening A background check will be required for employment in this position. Authorization to Work in the United States USI may sponsor an employment-related visa for this position. Interview Accommodations Persons with disabilities requiring accommodations in the application and interview process please contact the Associate Director of Human Resources, Constance Hermann, at cjhermann1@usi.edu or (812) 461-5363. Contacting the Associate Director of Human Resources is intended for use in seeking disability-related accommodations only. For general applicant inquiries, contact Human Resources at HumanRes@usi.edu or (812) 464-1815. EEO Statement USI is an Equal Opportunity Employer as to all protected groups, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities Recommended Jobs Assistant Cheer Coach Evansville, Indiana, United States Athletics Assistant Cheer Coach, part-time, non-benefit eligible Human Resources Business Partner Evansville, Indiana, United States Human Resources Human Resources Business Partner, full-time, benefits-eligible Dean, Kinney College of Nursing and Health Professions Evansville, Indiana, United States Kinney College of Nursing & Health Professions Dean, Kinney College of Nursing and Health Professions Assistant Professor of Nursing Evansville, Indiana, United States Kinney College of Nursing & Health Professions 10 month, tenure track Assistant Professor of Nursing. Assistant Professor of Marketing Evansville, Indiana, United States Romain College of Business 9-month, Tenure track Assistant Professor of Marketing Lecturer in World Languages and Cultures Evansville, Indiana, United States College of Liberal Arts Part-Time Lecturer in World Languages and Cultures Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Terms & Conditions Privacy Policy Candidate Details"
